<JobCoordinates>
  <!--
    Job coordinate points. Each point = one location + one function for the job loop.

    Common attributes:
      id, name, job, function, x, y, z, heading

    job:      TowTruck | FoodDelivery | Garbage | Bus
    function: per job, see vocabulary below.
    heading:  optional facing in degrees.

    Function vocabulary:
      TowTruck      TowDropoff          garage where a towed vehicle is delivered
      FoodDelivery  RestaurantPickup     restaurant: job garage, meal loading point and start of a run.
                                         site="<legacyKey>" links the point to its Sites.xml restaurant
                                         (role="Restaurant"): the site's marker, district, product
                                         commodity and ingredient stock win over the coordinates
                                         below, which are only the fallback anchor used when the site
                                         cannot be resolved. serviceRadius="5000" is the metre radius
                                         around the restaurant the job delivers inside. Keep it larger
                                         than the longest distance band or far customers never appear.
                    CustomerDropoff      one customer address of the shared delivery pool. The pool is
                                         shared on purpose: the job keeps the candidates that are
                                         inside the restaurant's serviceRadius and inside the rolled
                                         distance band, so one address can serve any restaurant that
                                         is close enough. district= must match Districts.xml.
      Garbage       GarbageDepot         depot: spawn garbage trucks, start/choose a route, and tip loads
      Bus           BusStop              passenger stop
                    BusDepot             route start/end depot

    Coordinates are example placeholders; replace with final locations.
  -->

